1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,383
Hans the Butcher: seven feet tall, a pig-faced iron mask, and a sledgehammer that

2
00:00:04,383 --> 00:00:05,996
could crush an elephant's skull.

3
00:00:06,216 --> 00:00:07,496
Here's how he plays.

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,787
Hans has no special setup and no special rules.

5
00:00:10,787 --> 00:00:15,127
He plays purely on the core rules, which makes him the ideal killer to learn with.

6
00:00:15,347 --> 00:00:19,658
He's slow and weak at low Bloodlust, but every Victim he kills makes him faster and

7
00:00:19,658 --> 00:00:20,125
deadlier.

8
00:00:20,933 --> 00:00:25,260
Watch his Dark Powers. With Dark Obsession, whenever he attacks you, he attacks an

9
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:25,840
extra time.

10
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:30,135
His Epic Dark Power, Blood Frenzy, punishes you for every Victim he kills.

11
00:00:30,355 --> 00:00:34,088
And his Hammer Rush Terror card hurts more for each Victim caught in the attack.

12
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:39,237
A few tips. He barely moves early on, so spend the opening turns rescuing Victims

13
00:00:39,237 --> 00:00:40,468
before he reaches them.

14
00:00:40,688 --> 00:00:45,061
A low-Bloodlust Hans is weak, so with a decent weapon you can stand and trade blows.

15
00:00:45,281 --> 00:00:47,551
If he gets strong anyway, he's predictable:

16
00:00:47,551 --> 00:00:51,511
cycle Guard and Retaliate. And never end your turn in or next to his space.

17
00:00:52,333 --> 00:00:56,778
On Final Girl Stats, Final Girls win about sixty-three percent of games against

18
00:00:56,778 --> 00:00:58,072
Hans, close to average.

19
00:00:58,292 --> 00:01:02,658
He's hardest at the Sacred Groves and the Carnival of Blood, and Dark Obsession is

20
00:01:02,658 --> 00:01:04,841
his most punishing Dark Power. Good luck.

